  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Capacity of Marginalized Human Rights Defenders Especially Women and Groups with Diverse Minority Identities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project benefits marginalized human rights defenders in Indonesia as an ODA eligible country who have less access to capacity building due to their location or area of work so that they understand protection instruments and acquire support to ensure their security in defending and promoting human rights. The project revolves round 4 types of activities, namely (1) Building collaboration with state human rights institutions, (2)  Developing public support through campaigns and public education with video documentaries, (3) Training for marginalized human rights defenders and (4) Preparation of mentoring for alumni of marginalized human rights defenders training.</narrative>
  </description>
